Problem Statement 
Manufacturing companies face daily operational challenges such as production delays, unexpected machine downtime, raw material shortages, product defects and delayed customer orders. Although factories collect large amounts of production, inventory, maintenance and quality data, this information is often distributed across separate databases, spreadsheets and reports. As a result, managers spend considerable time gathering information and identifying the causes of operational problems, delaying important decisions.
We propose DataMind Manufacturing, an AI-powered conversational data analysis system that enables factory managers and supervisors to ask questions about manufacturing operations in natural language. Using Google Gemma to interpret user questions and Snowflake to retrieve and analyze actual manufacturing data, the system provides evidence-backed answers, relevant records, executed SQL queries and understandable explanations. It also identifies missing information, handles ambiguous questions and avoids unsupported conclusions.
The goal is to make manufacturing data more accessible, improve operational visibility and help managers make faster, better-informed decisions using reliable data.
